# Architecture

## Stack
- **Backend:** Node.js + Express REST API (`backend/src/`)
- **Database:** SQLite (`data/pooja_shop.db`) — portable to PostgreSQL later
- **Frontend:** React + Vite (`frontend/src/`) — HTTP API calls only
- **Desktop:** Electron wraps backend + frontend (`electron/`)

## Rules
1. All business logic lives in the backend API, not the frontend.
2. Frontend must use `frontend/src/api/client.js` — never import DB or backend internals.
3. Future mobile/web clients reuse the same API — keep routes generic (use `shop_id` on records).
4. AI/Claude calls only from backend (`backend/src/services/advisorService.js`), never from frontend.
5. Reports/exports generated server-side (`exportService.js`).

## Folder map
```
backend/src/routes/     → REST endpoints
backend/src/services/   → business logic
backend/src/db/         → schema + queries
frontend/src/pages/     → screen components
frontend/src/api/       → HTTP client
```

## Currency & locale
- INR (₹), Indian number formatting
- Simple UI language for non-technical shop owners
